# syntek-base only — this file is copier-excluded, so a generated project never receives it.
#
# Every artefact under project-management/src/ is written AGAINST a user story that a real
# project has and this template does not. Anything authored here is therefore a test of the
# scaffolding — proving a template renders, a naming pattern holds, a workflow runs — and test
# artefacts belong to the session that made them, not to the template's git history and not to
# every project generated from it.
#
# A generated project is the opposite case: its stories, sprints, ADRs and plans ARE the work,
# and they stay tracked, which is what each folder's CONTEXT.md describes. That is why this rule
# must not travel with the template.
#
# The shape is an ALLOWLIST, deliberately. A denylist of artefact patterns fails by silently
# shipping a local test file into every generated project; an allowlist fails by silently not
# shipping a new template file, which the first generation reveals. Given the choice, the rule
# fails towards keeping the user's codebase clean.
#
# It also needs no edit when a numbered folder is added: every folder ships nothing but its
# documentation pair and its templates, both of which are matched by pattern below.

# Ignore everything...
*

# ...except this file, which must stay tracked or the rule vanishes on a fresh clone —
# and copier.yml can only exclude a file the template actually carries.
!.gitignore

# ...but descend into every directory, or none of the negations below is ever reached. Git does
# not look inside an excluded directory, so this line is load-bearing, not tidiness.
!*/

# The documentation pair every directory in this tree ships (docs-pairing.sh enforces it).
!CONTEXT.md
!CLAUDE.md

# Every per-story template — the shape a real artefact is written from. Matches at any depth,
# which covers the three-stage folders (04–08) and the PLANNING/IMPLEMENTATION pairs (09–13).
!*TEMPLATE*

# ── Named shipped content: real template files that carry no TEMPLATE in the name ────────────

# The asset pipeline and ClickUp sync scripts.
!00-ASSETS/scripts/*.sh

# The brand-guide and component-guide build sources (Python → LaTeX). The rendered PDFs are
# build output and are deliberately NOT re-included — a generated project builds its own.
!06-BRAND-GUIDE/guide-build/*.py
!06-BRAND-GUIDE/guide-build/*.tex
!07-COMPONENTS/component-build/*.py
!07-COMPONENTS/component-build/*.tex

# The stylesheet every wireframe links.
!08-WIREFRAMES/SHARED/wireframe.css

# The six GDPR register skeletons — filled in per project, but shipped as empty registers.
!09-GDPR/BREACH-NOTIFICATION.md
!09-GDPR/CONSENT-LAWFUL-BASIS.md
!09-GDPR/DATA-INVENTORY.md
!09-GDPR/DATA-SUBJECT-RIGHTS.md
!09-GDPR/RETENTION-DELETION.md
!09-GDPR/THIRD-PARTY-PROCESSORS.md

# The two test records are templates named for the story they are copied to, not for their role.
!17-TESTS/US000-MANUAL-TESTING.md
!17-TESTS/US000-TEST-STATUS.md

# The incident register's index — the one file in 22-INCIDENTS that is not an incident.
!22-INCIDENTS/INCIDENT-INDEX.md
